  <title>
    <media type="image" width="40px" height="40px" its:translate="no" src="figures/orca-logo.svg" /> Where Am I
  </title>
  <p>
    Where Am I presents information about your current location, such as the focused control,
    its state, and its position within a group.
  </p>
  <p>
    <em style="strong">Preferences location:</em>
    <gui>Commands</gui> category, <gui>Commands</gui> section, <gui>Object details</gui> group.
  </p>
  <section id="basic-and-detailed-where-am-i">
    <title>Basic and detailed Where Am I</title>
    <p>
      Basic Where Am I repeats information about the current item. Detailed Where Am I can add
      information about containing groups and other details. The information provided depends on
      the type of object and your current location. Some objects provide the same information
      for both commands.
    </p>
    <section id="commands-basic-and-detailed-where-am-i">
      <title>Commands</title>
      <list>
        <item>
          <p>
            <gui>Perform the basic Where Am I operation</gui>
          </p>
          <list>
            <item>
              <p>
                Desktop: <keyseq>
                  <key>Keypad Enter</key>
                </keyseq>
              </p>
            </item>
            <item>
              <p>
                Laptop: <keyseq>
                  <key>Orca Modifier</key>
                  <key>Enter</key>
                </keyseq>
              </p>
            </item>
          </list>
        </item>
        <item>
          <p>
            <gui>Perform the detailed Where Am I operation</gui>
          </p>
          <list>
            <item>
              <p>
                Desktop: <keyseq>
                  <key>Keypad Enter</key>
                </keyseq>
                (press twice)
              </p>
            </item>
            <item>
              <p>
                Laptop: <keyseq>
                  <key>Orca Modifier</key>
                  <key>Enter</key>
                </keyseq>
                (press twice)
              </p>
            </item>
          </list>
        </item>
      </list>
    </section>
  </section>
